# 🤝 Handling Leadership Pushback When SLOs Threaten Velocity

---

# 🎯 Core Philosophy

SRE is about balancing:

```text id="3otjlwm"
reliability + delivery speed
```

not maximizing one at the expense of the other.

---

# ✅ My Approach

---

# 1. Use Error Budgets

Instead of subjective debate:

* define SLOs
* track error budget consumption

This creates:

```text id="4e3vmz"
data-driven engineering decisions
```

---

# 2. Quantify Business Impact

Translate outages into:

* revenue impact
* customer churn
* SLA penalties
* operational cost

Leadership responds better to:

```text id="ol7r1w"
business risk
```

than technical fear.

---

# 3. Avoid “No”

Instead of blocking releases:

* propose phased rollout
* canary deployment
* feature flags
* controlled blast radius

---

# 4. Prioritize Reliability Debt

Explain:

* reliability debt compounds
* outages reduce delivery velocity later
* unstable platforms slow teams permanently

---

# 5. Create Shared Ownership

Reliability should NOT belong only to SRE.

Shared ownership between:

* platform teams
* developers
* product leadership

---

# 🎯 Real Production Example

If production stability declines:

* tighten deployment guardrails
* reduce rollout size
* increase observability
* require canary validation

but avoid:

```text id="8pdj0r"
freezing innovation completely
```

